  nodePositions: []
  nodeAbstract: 
  nodeTextLayers:
  - GLP1-R's seven helices are all alpha helices.
  - Alpha helices are always right handed; Each turn is approximately 3.6 amino acids
    in length.
  - Membrane-spanning alpha helices are the most common structural motif in membrane
    proteins like GLP1-R.
  - When GLP1 is bound to GLP1-R, there is an observable kink in the structure of
    one of GLP1-R's helices.
